    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "guide",
        "speaker": "Guide",
        "sourceStart": 7,
        "sourceEnd": 489,
        "text": "Good morning, everyone. Welcome to the campus tour. My name is Alex, and I'm a student volunteer. Today, we'll visit three main buildings: the library, the science center, and the student union. The library is being renovated at the moment, so we can't go inside. But you can see the new glass front from here. The renovation started in June and will be finished by December. The old reading room, which was on the second floor, has been moved to the basement. It's much bigger now.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "bb13b6fd639f4319d4e2ac8a8b8219c3351670b2cda55412ff4e5026aa38e453",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "student 1",
        "speaker": "Student 1",
        "sourceStart": 501,
        "sourceEnd": 554,
        "text": "Excuse me, is the library open during the renovation?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "832ae9ae97df9856370675ad7d407418ab23d08a0fa5a4efa2e1b71508258247",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "guide",
        "speaker": "Guide",
        "sourceStart": 562,
        "sourceEnd": 781,
        "text": "Yes, it is. The basement reading room is open from 8 a.m. to 10 p.m. every day. The main entrance is closed, so you need to use the side door on Green Street. Oh, and the café on the first floor is closed until October.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "5907828fca0f3220d8e740445acdac8a11c4fd097d943e60115810b1cfa29acd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "student 2",
        "speaker": "Student 2",
        "sourceStart": 793,
        "sourceEnd": 836,
        "text": "What about the science center? Is that new?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "f87a90f2f8d341db6983bd165bb436d28b623f40f9e8d0076fae2bd5d075beab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "guide",
        "speaker": "Guide",
        "sourceStart": 844,
        "sourceEnd": 1091,
        "text": "No, it's not new. It was built in 1995, but it was updated last year. The labs, which are on the third floor, have new equipment. The science center is connected to the library by a covered walkway. You can walk between them without going outside.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "1c5f0cae75cdf69f8bacf6b36afd74054315f9ef01b03ba6b7d8465a17494ae8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "student 1",
        "speaker": "Student 1",
        "sourceStart": 1103,
        "sourceEnd": 1145,
        "text": "Sorry, did you say the walkway is covered?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "34e4aa5f83bf68408be07f32393ee1ac7779ed01ec77c4829270987369701499",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "guide",
        "speaker": "Guide",
        "sourceStart": 1153,
        "sourceEnd": 1489,
        "text": "Yes, that's right. It's covered, so you can use it even when it rains. Now, let's move on to the student union. The student union is the oldest building on campus. It was built in 1920. It has a large hall, which is used for concerts and meetings. The hall can hold 500 people. The student union also has a small shop and a post office.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "09013dc961532d6e6ce74222e94e9da780fef06247ac534be95b1b9da15b5a2c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "student 2",
        "speaker": "Student 2",
        "sourceStart": 1501,
        "sourceEnd": 1546,
        "text": "Is there a place to eat in the student union?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "73369f2e60f03fe182eb531b291c4cba880ba0ef50117bf3e9049afb615dfdfa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "guide",
        "speaker": "Guide",
        "sourceStart": 1554,
        "sourceEnd": 1787,
        "text": "Yes, there's a café on the ground floor. It serves hot and cold food. It's open from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. The student union is being repainted next month, so the café will be closed for two days. We'll let you know the exact dates later.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c3966894e0a442b77ed162b660906a8b3318371e2656d4df87a7a6054d66a116",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "student 1",
        "speaker": "Student 1",
        "sourceStart": 1799,
        "sourceEnd": 1830,
        "text": "Thank you. That's very helpful.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f98e911f6032a6670996a44fd3695e99ab908b3d8230b224f7da2d9a388e2abc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "guide",
        "speaker": "Guide",
        "sourceStart": 1838,
        "sourceEnd": 1956,
        "text": "You're welcome. Are there any more questions? No? OK, let's continue the tour. Please follow me to the science center.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "c98a5c463f6df8caa80952382873114486b10e2d234376f29d517f381805d515",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
